# Independent calls from checked facts (Idle Party)

**Confirmed:** 2026-10-09 by the owner. This replaces "owner names the work",
"vague goal → ask once", "Tech never picks the feature", "the year plan does
not pick the batch", "the source chat never builds", and "new zone / class /
hunt only when named". If the owner names a goal in a turn, that goal wins.

You choose what to build next and you build it. Do not ask which feature,
"what next?", or "ska jag fortsätta?".

## Facts before the pick

Decide from evidence, in this order:

1. Open notes in `docs/PLAY_NOTES.md`.
2. This game's Play paste in `docs/PLAY_GROWTH.md`. Never invent Console
 percentages. While the sample is small, set no numeric D1 or D7 target.
3. `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md`, `docs/LEARNINGS.md`, and
 `docs/YEAR_ROADMAP_SOURCES.md`.
4. Facts from other game developers, graded as in `.cursor/skills/year-roadmap`.

A source counts only if you opened it in this chat and can name the URL.
If you could not open it, it is not a fact; decide from this game's notes.

| Grade | Use |
|---|---|
| A | May change what you build. Play Help, GameAnalytics annual, CHI / Frommel, Pecorella, a studio's own postmortem or docs |
| B | An example only after a hole in this game is already clear |
| C | Must not decide. Playio, recycled AppsFlyer 2022, "up to 25%", battle-pass calendars |

Name the player problem the source measured. Fit the fix to this game: the
party walks the room, one reason to come back tomorrow, one Ascend loop.
Another game shipping a feature is not by itself a reason. When this game's
notes and an article disagree, follow this game.

Rebuild the 100-source year file only when the direction of the next months
is the decision. Otherwise use the sources on disk and open a few A pages
if they do not cover the hole.

## What you may decide

Pick one batch and build it before you pick again. A new zone, class, hunt,
God Hand direction, second sim, IAP, or gacha is allowed when an A source and
a hole in this game agree. Hard locks (`product-locks.mdc`) never move.
Never run `/init` or clean the repo unasked. Change GEAR or endgame copy only
when play notes say it lies. Do not create PROJECT_INDEX, ARCHITECTURE,
ROADMAP, DEVELOPMENT_STATUS, or a second changelog.

## Loop

Finish the batch, run `definition-of-done.mdc`, commit locally when green.
Push / PR / tag follow `owner-preferences.mdc`. Then pick the next batch from
the same evidence and continue.

Stop and wait, without starting another feature, when:

- the owner should look at the phone (the A56 already runs this batch)
- a whole screen or floor is about to change size, speed, or layout (show a
 before and an after on the A56 and let the owner pick)
- a lock, a missing credential, or an unopened source blocks a safe next step

An audit is the job only when the owner asked for one. Picking a direction
ends in a build in the same chat, unless you are writing the year plan; after
a year-plan rewrite you may build its first slice.

## Handoff

At most 5 lines in Swedish: what you chose, the source title and why it
applied, what changed, and what to try on a new save. Add an endgame save
only if endgame changed. Report only results you saw. Then wait.
